:Geomorphology-agent
    a skos:Collection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition "Geomorphological agents that play a role in producing distinctive landform elements."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:member
        :Geomorphology-agent-bio ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-extra ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-gravity ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-ice ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-internal ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-precipitation ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-stand ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-streamflow ,
        :Geomorphology-agent-wind ;
    skos:note """Much of the standard terminology relevant to landform elements presumes that the geomorphological agent responsible for a landform is known; this presumption has been explicitly incorporated in the following glossary. In practice, the observer may find it difficult to infer correctly the agent responsible for producing a given landform element. The problem may be compounded by the apparent significance of more than one agent. In such cases, the observer should record both (a) the dominant agent, or the agent that is confidently inferred; and (b) a subordinate agent, or an agent that is dubiously inferred. In dubious cases, leave category (a) blank.
The importance of identifying landform elements with the agent channelled stream flow is discussed under ‘Channel depth relative to width’ on page 39.""" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Geomorphological agent"@en ;
.

