:landform-pattern-CAL
    a
        skos:Concept ,
        :Landform-pattern-name ;
    dcterms:relation
        :landform-pattern-CAL-occasional-elements ,
        :landform-pattern-CAL-typical-elements ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition """rare landform pattern typically of very high relief and steep to precipitous slope. It is without stream channels or has fixed, erosional channels forming a centripetal, integrated tributary pattern. The landform has subsided or was excavated as a result of volcanism. 
rare landform pattern typically of very high relief and steep to precipitous slope. It is without stream channels or has fixed, erosional channels forming a centripetal, integrated tributary pattern. The landform has subsided or was excavated as a result of volcanism.
Typical elements: scarp, hillslope, lake.
Occasional elements: cone, hillcrest, stream channel."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:notation "CAL" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Caldera"@en ;
    skos:related
        :relief-class-M ,
        :slope-class-PR ,
        :slope-class-ST ,
        :slope-class-VS ;
    skos:topConceptOf cs: ;
.

:landform-pattern-COR
    a
        skos:Concept ,
        :Landform-pattern-name ;
    dcterms:relation
        :landform-pattern-COR-common-elements ,
        :landform-pattern-COR-typical-elements ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition """continuously active or relict landform pattern built up to the sea level of the present day or of a former time by corals and other organisms. It is mainly level, with moderately inclined to precipitous slopes below the sea level. Stream channels are generally absent, but there may occasionally be fixed, deep, erosional tidal stream channels forming a disintegrated non-tributary pattern. 
Typical elements: reef flat, lagoon, cliff (submarine).
Common elements: beach, beach ridge."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:notation "COR" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coral reef"@en ;
    skos:related
        :slope-class-LE ,
        :slope-class-MO ,
        :slope-class-PR ,
        :slope-class-ST ,
        :slope-class-VS ;
    skos:topConceptOf cs: ;
.

:landform-pattern-COR-common-elements
    a skos:Collection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition "Common elements of Coral reef"@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:member
        :landform-element-BEA ,
        :landform-element-BRI ;
    skos:prefLabel "Common elements of Coral reef"@en ;
    skos:related :landform-pattern-COR ;
.

:landform-pattern-FLO-occasional-elements
    a skos:Collection ;
