:landform-pattern-DUN
    a
        skos:Concept ,
        :Landform-pattern-name ;
    dcterms:relation
        :landform-pattern-DUN-common-elements ,
        :landform-pattern-DUN-included-patterns ,
        :landform-pattern-DUN-typical-elements ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition """level to rolling landform pattern of very low or extremely low relief without stream channels, built up or locally excavated, eroded or aggraded by wind. 
Typical elements: dune or dunecrest, duneslope, swale, blow-out, risecrest, residual rise, riseslope.
Common elements: hummocky dune, barchan dune, parabolic dune, linear dune.
Included types of landform pattern are: longitudinal dunefield, parabolic dunefield."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:notation "DUN" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dunefield"@en ;
    skos:related
        :relief-class-P ,
        :relief-class-R ,
        :slope-class-GE ,
        :slope-class-LE ,
        :slope-class-MO ,
        :slope-class-VG ;
    skos:topConceptOf cs: ;
.

:landform-pattern-ESC
    a
        skos:Concept ,
        :Landform-pattern-name ;
    dcterms:relation
        :landform-pattern-ESC-common-elements ,
        :landform-pattern-ESC-occasional-elements ,
        :landform-pattern-ESC-typical-elements ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition """steep to precipitous landform pattern forming a linearly extensive, straight or sinuous, inclined surface, which separates terrains at different altitudes; a plateau is commonly above the escarpment. Relief within the landform pattern may be high (hilly) or low (planar). The upper margin is often marked by an included cliff or scarp. 
Typical elements: hillcrest, hillslope, cliff-footslope.
Common elements: cliff, scarp, scarp-footslope, talus, footslope, alcove.
Occasional element: stream bed."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:notation "ESC" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Escarpment"@en ;
    skos:related
        :relief-class-H ,
        :relief-class-L ,
        :slope-class-PR ,
        :slope-class-ST ,
        :slope-class-VS ;
    skos:topConceptOf cs: ;
.

